Package: faperu
Title: Access and Design-Based Analysis of Peruvian Official Surveys and Censuses
Version: 0.4.2
Authors@R: c(
    person("Fred", "Torres Cruz", role = "aut",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0003-0834-6834")),
    person("Richar Andre", "Vilca Solorzano", email = "andrevilcasolorzano@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"), comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0003-2385-5263"))
  )
Description: One catalog, one download function and a few helpers to read,
    weight, locate and analyse ten Peruvian official data sources: ENAHO,
    ENDES, ENA, EPEN, ENAPRES, ENUT, ENARES and the Annual Economic Survey
    from INEI, the School Census from MINEDU (ESCALE) and the 2017 National
    Censuses. Files are cached and checked with SHA-256, and new survey years
    are detected from the INEI microdata portal
    <https://proyectos.inei.gob.pe/microdatos/>. Design-based estimates of
    means, proportions and totals come with standard errors, confidence
    intervals and the coefficient-of-variation quality bands used by INEI;
    seven ready indicators reproduce INEI's published figures; estimates from
    several surveys can be linked by district and year and drawn as maps and
    tables. This package is independent and is not affiliated with INEI or
    MINEDU.
